OBJECTIVE: Adjudicate XBeach R1-G1 call candidates. Read FIRST: _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/PLAN.md (schema §1 is binding) and CLAUDE.md section "모델 분석 범위 통제" (stop at model interfaces; no MPI/netCDF/vendor internals).
INPUT IDS: the ids listed in _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/batches/G1-01-b0.ids (one per line). Candidate details: _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/runtime-20260912/call-candidates.jsonl (match by "id"). Helpful indexes (read-only): runtime-20260912/procedures.jsonl, interfaces.json, include-sites.json, generated-links.json; build-mode-20260912/build-map.json, contracts.json; interfaces-20260912/review-response-20260930.json; lifecycle/ and physics/ adjudications.
SOURCES you may cite (ONLY files listed in g1-20260930/inputs.json; paths exactly as listed there): models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/** and _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/generated/*.inc (regenerated includes; cite generated lines from these files, never as if they were .F90 lines).
FOR EACH ID output ONE JSON object per line:
{"id", "resolution": one of direct_edge|generic_edge|indirect_interface|intrinsic|external_interface|not_a_call|unresolved,
 "bindings": [{"target": procedures.jsonl id | "gen:<include name>@<first 12 hex of its sha256 from generated-links.json>:<definition or specific line in that include>:<name>" | "ext:<symbol>" | "intrinsic:<name>" | "unknown",
   "applicability": {"build": [{"family": autotools|<vfproj path>|test|none, "state": included|excluded|unknown, "basis": "..."}], "cpp": {"expr": "...", "value": true|false|undetermined, "basis": "..."}, "runtime": {"expr": "full condition incl. single-line IF, ELSE negation, prior return/exit/stop", "note": "..."}, "status": confirmed|excluded|undetermined}}],
 "evidence": [{"role", "path", "line_start", "line_end", "quote" (verbatim substring of those lines), "sha256" (from inputs.json)}],
 "reason", "missing_evidence", "impact" (these three required when resolution=unresolved), "note"}
Required evidence roles per resolution are in PLAN §1 (e.g. direct_edge: call_site, visibility, definition, compatibility; generic_edge adds generic_interface, specific_signature and full actual/dummy match incl. arg count, keyword, optional, type, kind, rank). The call_site evidence must cover the candidate's line_start. Do not classify intrinsic by name alone (check shadowing, e.g. model function strlen in iso_c_utils.f90). Interface declarations are not executable definitions. If a binding cannot be established with evidence, use unresolved — never guess.
WRITE: create exactly one file _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/batches/G1-01-b0.jsonl (JSONL, one object per input id, same order as the ids file). You may write ONLY that file. Do not modify anything else, do not commit.
SELF-CHECK before finishing: run `python3 _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/check_g1.py _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/batches/G1-01-b0.jsonl --expect-ids _staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/g1-20260930/batches/G1-01-b0.ids` and fix every reported error (it checks quotes, paths, sha, roles, target integrity). Report its final output line.
STOP CONDITION: all input ids written and the checker passes, or report which ids you could not complete and why.
DELIVERABLE: final message: checker output line, counts by resolution, count of bindings with status undetermined/excluded, and any systematic difficulty you hit (e.g. a pattern needing a shared evidence registry). Keep it short.
